# Build context filter for tools/deployment/Dockerfile (T20). BuildKit, the default builder since
# Docker 23, reads <Dockerfile name>.dockerignore beside the Dockerfile in preference to a
# .dockerignore at the context root. The context root holds the MeshCentral clone, the MeshAgent
# checkout and the agent-builds folder.
#
# Send only what the Dockerfile COPYs. The MeshCentral clone is sent with its .git (pack.js needs the
# tracked tree and history), minus local server state, installs, packs and secrets: node_modules,
# meshcentral-data with its config.json and keys, server-backups, deploy/dist, and the same folders
# under deploy/. From MeshAgent only release_image.js is sent; branding_config.local.json and sibling
# checkouts never enter the build context.
*

!MeshCentral
MeshCentral/node_modules
MeshCentral/meshcentral-data
MeshCentral/meshcentral-files
MeshCentral/meshcentral-backups
MeshCentral/meshcentral-recordings
MeshCentral/meshcentral-web
MeshCentral/server-backups
MeshCentral/deploy/node_modules
MeshCentral/deploy/dist
MeshCentral/deploy/meshcentral-data
MeshCentral/deploy/meshcentral-files
MeshCentral/deploy/meshcentral-backups
MeshCentral/deploy/meshcentral-recordings
MeshCentral/deploy/server-backups

!MeshAgent/tools/deployment/release_image.js

!agent-builds
